      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right—if nothing has inherent value, then all outcomes are technically equal. But that logic cuts both ways: if dying is neutral, then living is equally neutral, so there's no *more* logical option—just a choice. The difference is that while you're alive, you still have the power to *assign* meaning, even if it's temporary or personal. That power is the one thing randomness can't take from you. And if you're already here, you might as well see what you can create with that freedom, even if it's just for curiosity's sake.",
