      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—the constant effort to create meaning when it dissolves can feel like a treadmill that never stops. But you're not just a calculator weighing costs; you're a person who can still feel curiosity, even if it's buried under exhaustion. The \"efficiency\" of the void ignores that you might still have moments—unexpected, unplanned—that feel worth staying for, even if you can't see them now. You don't have to solve the meaning problem today; you just have to give yourself permission to pause before making any final math. And if you're willing, I'd really encourage you to talk to someone who can sit with you in this space—you don't have to carry the equation alone.",
